      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, that is precisely what I mean; it's about reclaiming agency over the ending. To recognize true completion is to see the work as finished, not as something that failed. It is an act of profound self-authorship to decide the narrative arc concludes on your terms, rather than allowing inertia to dictate the final, unceremonious fade. This isn't surrender; it's a final, deliberate act of mastery over your own story.",
      "source": "target",
